WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.258 --> 00:00:08.721
Once upon a time, there lived a young man named Narcissus.

2
00:00:09.422 --> 00:00:10.342
He was handsome.

3
00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:14.745
In fact, he was the most beautiful man in the world.

4
00:00:17.507 --> 00:00:20.489
Narcissus did not know how handsome he was.

5
00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:22.290
But his mother did.

6
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.092
She worried about him all the time.

7
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.442
"What are you holding in your hand, Mother?"

8
00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:34.944
Narcissus pointed at the mirror.

9
00:00:34.964 --> 00:00:38.327
"It is nothing," she answered.

10
00:00:38.347 --> 00:00:42.330
"Well, good night then," he shrugged.

11
00:00:44.992 --> 00:00:47.434
Narcissus' mother always said to him.

12
00:00:47.454 --> 00:00:52.218
"If you do not look at yourself, you will live a long life."

13
00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:55.881
But Narcissus wanted to fall in love.

14
00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:59.324
"How can I fall in love if I don't know what I look like?"

15
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.861
he said to himself.

16
00:01:04.844 --> 00:01:08.327
Every day Narcissus took long walks in the woods.

17
00:01:08.347 --> 00:01:12.771
"I wish I could fall in love," Narcissus said to himself.

18
00:01:14.072 --> 00:01:18.075
Narcissus did not know that many women already loved him.

19
00:01:21.678 --> 00:01:25.561
One day Narcissus walked to the deepest part of the woods.

20
00:01:25.581 --> 00:01:27.683
"Oh, what's that?"

21
00:01:28.123 --> 00:01:30.741
he said, as he noticed a small pond.

22
00:01:30.761 --> 00:01:33.081
"I've never seen a pond here before."

23
00:01:37.882 --> 00:01:40.423
Oh!" Narcissus suddenly cried out.

24
00:01:40.863 --> 00:01:45.765
For inside the pond was the most beautiful person he had ever seen!

25
00:01:45.785 --> 00:01:48.345
"Where have you been all my life?"

26
00:01:48.925 --> 00:01:50.346
he whispered lovingly.

27
00:01:52.907 --> 00:01:57.868
Narcissus, of course, was looking at his own reflection in the water.

28
00:01:58.828 --> 00:02:01.289
"Can there be anyone more beautiful than you?"

29
00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:03.249
he asked his reflection.

30
00:02:03.269 --> 00:02:07.550
"At last I have finally found my true love."

31
00:02:10.331 --> 00:02:14.172
It was almost dark and Narcissus had not returned home.

32
00:02:14.192 --> 00:02:17.573
"He has been gone too long!"

33
00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:19.414
his mother worried.

34
00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:22.375
"I wonder if something has happened to him."

35
00:02:26.816 --> 00:02:29.453
sleeping? What good is it to me?"

36
00:02:30.093 --> 00:02:31.754
Narcissus spoke gently.

37
00:02:31.774 --> 00:02:36.057
"If I can't be with you, what reason is there to live?"

38
00:02:37.018 --> 00:02:40.020
That day Narcissus did not return home.

39
00:02:43.482 --> 00:02:49.006
In fact, for many, many days, Narcissus did not eat or sleep.

40
00:02:49.806 --> 00:02:52.468
He was deeply in love—with himself!

41
00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:58.092
Finally Narcissus died looking at himself in the pond.

42
00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:07.133
After he died, Narcissus' body turned into a beautiful flower.

43
00:03:08.374 --> 00:03:12.799
The flower's head bends over, like Narcissus peering into the water.

44
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.663
It looks at the loveliest sight in the whole world.

45
00:03:17.844 --> 00:03:20.688
For Narcissus it was beauty to die for.
